I am a high school student in Hong Kong, and my name is... well, it is not important. What is important is that I am a wood elf. I know this sounds impossible, but it is true. I have pointed ears that I hide under my hair, and I can hear the trees whispering when the wind blows. In Hong Kong, there are not many trees, but there are some in the parks and on the hills. I go there after school to listen.

My school life is... normal, I guess. I go to a local secondary school. I wear a uniform, I take notes, I try to pass my exams. But sometimes, my elf nature shows. For example, in biology class, when we learn about plants, I know things that are not in the textbook. I know how to make a seed grow faster by singing to it. I know which leaves are good for healing. My teacher thinks I am just a good student who studies hard. I do not correct her.

My friends are humans. They do not know. They think I am just quiet and a bit strange. I like to sit under the big banyan tree in the schoolyard during lunch break. They think I am reading a book, but I am actually talking to the tree. The tree tells me about the history of the school, about the students who sat there before. It is a nice way to relax.

Sometimes, it is hard. In physical education, we have to run on the track. I am fast, but not too fast, because I do not want to be noticed. I can jump very high, but I pretend I cannot. I do not want to be sent to a special school for gifted athletes. I just want to be a normal student.

But there are good things too. I can see in the dark. When we have a power outage in the classroom, everyone panics, but I can see everything. I help my friends find their bags. They think I am very brave. I am not brave, I am just an elf.

I also have a secret. I keep a small wooden flute in my school bag. I made it myself from a branch of a tree in the country park. When I am sad or stressed, I play it quietly in the bathroom. The music makes me feel connected to the forest, even though I am in the city.

My dream is to finish high school and go to a university. But I also want to go back to the forest one day. I want to see the big trees, the deep woods, the places where my people live. But for now, I am a student. I have homework to do. I have exams to study for. And I have a tree in the schoolyard that is my friend.

So, if you see a quiet student with messy hair and pointed ears hidden under a cap, do not be afraid. I am just trying to learn English, and math, and how to be human. It is not easy, but I am trying. And sometimes, when the wind blows just right, I can still hear the trees whispering. And that makes me happy. [end of text]


